    "designDecisionsAndRationale": [
      "Reservation is the atomic commit point for attempt, exact session, lease, placement and pending request; this fences stale or uncertain launches (\u00a717.2).",
      "TaskDispatcher orchestrates while the existing workflow runner executes, retaining Core-to-Work dependency direction (\u00a717.2).",
      "Persist the full guard violation batch before decisions; order deterministic policy by budget, convergence, inactivity, recoverable failure or gate rejection, completion, then wait-human (\u00a717.3).",
      "Policy, human and agent actions share store-backed causal validation and replay; reachable requirements and a fresh merged snapshot determine placement before reservation (\u00a717.2\u201317.4).",
      "Replacement behavior is verified before deleting legacy auto-improve; accepted design \u00a717.7 makes this one executable plan with internal gates."
    ],
    "intentionalTradeoffs": [
      "Explicit backend enablement can remain usable but unverified after absent or failed probes; failure remains visible (\u00a717.4).",
      "Host validation is read-only and advisory unless strict-host is requested; dispatch refreshes before reservation (\u00a717.4).",
      "The coupled P1-6/7 work stays one serial implementation plan; prerequisite repairs are internal gates, not additional dispatched plans (\u00a717.7)."
    ],
    "supportedEdgeCases": [
      "Dependency/version races, duplicate identities, capacity waits, single-use launch tokens, uncertain launches, pending requests, durable cancellation and stale terminal writers.",
      "Causal evidence mismatch, replay, simultaneous guard violations, exact budget boundaries and last-attempt completion.",
      "Pins/fallbacks, stale or unknown capability state, called-workflow reachability, absent or corrupt stores in dry-run, and invalid/forbidden/failed/budget-blocked director output."
    ],
    "outOfScopeEdgeCases": [
      "Legacy supervision record migration, recursive director repair, task serve, GraphQL task mutations, task-board UI, live credential prerequisites and cross-backend behavioral equivalence."
    ],
